{"seq":20,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T16:27:08.349Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"defcea4f9f9fbdcd19a5a01e815a1d8b07bca45246709628a19f580700116891","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Dana, I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. #4419: gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet). The same note says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Heads-up: Marcus's July 2025 note describes #4419 as Gate 3 printer lag, so the ticket description may need checking against support.\n\n2. PD-4492: Pemberline Dock gatehouse kiosk SMS alerts at the Eau Claire yard, submitted by Thea on 4 Oct 2025. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday). Support patched it on 5 Oct, and the note has a follow-up to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\nMoss's other notes have no QFL ticket numbers. The two numbers in the Central handoffs note (#4409, #4412) belong to Pree's dealer account, so I left them out. I haven't written anything to the weekly notes; this list is for you to copy."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":21,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T16:27:16.297Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"158f2625491a6148ea1c701866a8f53257d90d640c719a5443d734a0cfcbcb73","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"I posted the list in your DM. It has two Quarrendon ticket numbers from Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#4419**: gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\". Moss's July 2025 handoff describes #4419 as Gate 3 printer lag, so check the description with support before you write it up.\n2. **PD-4492**: Pemberline Dock gatehouse kiosk SMS alerts at Eau Claire, submitted by Thea on 4 Oct 2025. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (2025-10-05).\n\nI left out #4409 and #4412 from the Central handoffs note, since they belong to Pree's dealer account, not Quarrendon.\n\nOther Quarrendon ticket numbers appear in the North weeklies and in your own notes (#8841 / PD-8841, #4819, #4812, #4912, NORTH-241, PD-4827). They aren't in Moss's notes, so I didn't include them. Tell me if you want them added.\n\nI haven't written anything to the weekly notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
